        "original_id": "daf91151-3a8f-51ed-a031-76ae76491ab1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: Mmm Papi, La Isla Bonita, Whiplash, Rock Me In\n- People: Madonna, Patrick Leonard, Bruce Gaitsch\n- Artists and Groups: Selena Gomez & the Scene, Destinee & Paris\n- Albums: True Blue\n- Concepts: Latin pop influence, musical influences\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, Madonna released \"La Isla Bonita\" on her third studio album \"True Blue\".\n- In 1987, \"La Isla Bonita\" was noted as a Latin pop song by Madonna.\n- Madonna and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced \"La Isla Bonita\", and Bruce Gaitsch contributed additional songwriting.\n- \"Mmm Papi\" is noted for having a Latin pop influence similar to Madonna's \"La Isla Bonita\".\n- The same writers created \"Mmm Papi\", \"Rock Me In\", and \"Whiplash\" for Selena Gomez & the Scene.\n- Destinee & Paris are sisters born and raised in New Jersey and based in Los Angeles.\n- Destinee & Paris cited Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Beyoncé, Katy Perry, Rihanna, and Gwen Stefani as influences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
